      "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/humming_bird\">@Humming_Bird</a></p>\n<p>This can happens when:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Company Currency vs. Account Currency</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>ERPNext always reports balances in your <strong>Company Default Currency</strong> (set in <em>Company master</em>).</li>\n<li>If the account (or transactions in it) are in a different currency, ERPNext shows both:\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>account currency balance</strong> (e.g., USD).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/8/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/8/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae_2_690x328.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"1e6rrvqnITpsh5T0P4Ic8UqsHtY\" width=\"690\" height=\"328\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/8/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae_2_690x328.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/8/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae_2_1035x492.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/8/089a512de5e484714b8b0c1d51d1d20df555a6ae_2_1380x656.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FBF9F6\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1718×819 79.2 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<pre><code>* The **converted balance in Company Currency** (e.g., PKR).\n</code></pre>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>Exchange Rate Issue</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>If the exchange rate between USD → PKR is set as <strong>1</strong>, ERPNext will show the <strong>same number</strong> in both currencies.</li>\n<li>This looks like what’s happening in your screenshot — the amounts are the same because ERPNext thinks <strong>1 USD = 1 PKR</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Why only some accounts show both currencies</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Accounts that are set as “Multi-currency” or have foreign-currency transactions will show both.</li>\n<li>Others show only the company currency.</li>\n</ul>",
